      "answer": "$x=2.46$ (3 s.f.).",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "Use a correct law for the logarithm of a product or power - *M1. Not available after incorrect manipulation, e.g. $6^{x+1}=12^{2x-3}$.\n\nObtain $\\ln3+(x+1)\\ln2=\\ln4+(2x-3)\\ln3$ - A1; or equivalent with no powers.\n\nSolve for $x$ - DM1, e.g. $x=\\dfrac{\\ln(2/81)}{\\ln(2/9)}$; allow evaluated logarithms.\n\nObtain $2.46$ only - A1.\n\nAlternative method: use a correct indices law for a product or power - *M1, e.g. $2^{x+1}=2\\times2^x$; not available after incorrect manipulation. $4=2^2$ alone is insufficient. Obtain $(2/9)^x=2/81$ - A1 (or equivalent powers of $x$ only, e.g. $6\\times2^x=(4/27)\\times9^x$; $(3^x)^2$ is not far enough). Solve for $x$ - DM1, e.g. $x=\\dfrac{\\ln(2/81)}{\\ln(2/9)}$ or $x=\\ln_{2/9}(2/81)$; obtain $2.46$ only - A1.\n\nPrinted total: 4.",
